node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store

# Machine-local registry now lives in ~/.boss/registry.json (not in the repo).
# Ignore any stray legacy copy so local project paths never get committed again.
registry/projects.json

# ── THREE tiers. Only two were ever declared, so the third became the default sink. ──
#
#   1. LOCAL       — everything listed below. The dogfood workspace: roadmap, research,
#                    strategy, design. Never leaves this machine.
#                    EXCEPT the conscience EVAL SUITE, moved to tier 2 by DEC-013 (v0.213.0):
#                    the cases and runners are TESTS, not strategy, and four public claims about
#                    BOSS's own rigour were resting on evidence no reader could open. The
#                    recorded transcripts stay LOCAL — the voice-hash already marks them STALE
#                    when a frame is edited, so tracking them means carrying expiring output.
#   2. PUBLIC REPO — tracked here and rendered to the website, installed NOWHERE:
#                    docs/GUIDE.md, GUIDE-teams, CHEATSHEET, SKILLS, MENTORS, HUMANE,
#                    PATTERNS — plus site/, web/ and registry/boundary.json.
#   3. INSTALLED   — what a founder actually receives: package.json `files:` (bin/ src/
#                    stages/ library/ VERSION PRINCIPLES.md registry/CHANGELOG.md
#                    registry/supersedes.json) plus README.md, which npm always includes.
#
# THIS COMMENT USED TO BE WRONG, and the error was load-bearing. It said the repo shipped
# "GUIDE, CHEATSHEET, SKILLS, MENTORS, IDS" as user-facing docs. Six of those are tier 2 and
# have never been in the tarball. Only IDS.md reaches a founder, and it does so as a scaffold
# template — not as a package file. Nine shipped mentor agents sent founders to MENTORS.md on
# the strength of this sentence. `check:refs` class 3b now fails on that, so the tiers cannot
# quietly disagree again; `check:boundary` does the same for agents and skills.
#
# Everything below is the dogfood workspace — roadmap, research, strategy, design.
docs/business/
docs/RESUME.md
docs/devlog.md
docs/evidence/
# docs/decisions/ is DELIBERATELY ABSENT from this list — the one record class BOSS publishes.
# A DEC's stated job is "the rationale future-you and a cofounder can read instead of guessing",
# and 49 citations of them sit in registry/CHANGELOG.md, which ships inside the npm package. They
# contain no personal, customer or financial content; the decision to publish was made per-record
# on the 16 that existed, and is NOT a standing rule — a future DEC that should stay private stays
# untracked, and check-refs handles its citation automatically (docs/IDS.md).
docs/ideas/
docs/extractions/
docs/research/
docs/source/
docs/dossier/
docs/design/
docs/fable-campaign/
docs/architecture/*
!docs/architecture/conscience-evals/
docs/architecture/conscience-evals/judgment/transcripts/
docs/exports/
docs/loops/
docs/mentor-practitioners.md

# BOSS's own dev workspace — root-anchored (leading slash) so the SHIPPED product
# templates under stages/*/template/.claude/ and their CLAUDE.md stay public.
# NOTE: gitignore has no inline comments — keep each pattern on its own line.
/CLAUDE.md
/.claude/
/.boss/
/bossbuild.code-workspace

# Fallout from hand-testing the Homebrew formula: an unexpanded template variable used as a real
# path. `npm install --prefix '{{HOMEBREW_PREFIX}}'` creates it as a literal directory, complete
# with lib/node_modules and share/man, in whatever cwd you ran it from. Empty, untracked and one
# `git add -A` from being committed. `npm run bump:formula` exists so nobody hand-runs that again.
{{HOMEBREW_PREFIX}}/

# Cloudflare deploy artifact — hand-zipped from site/ at deploy time, never source.
# Regenerate: cd site && zip -r ../site.zip . -x '.*' -x '__MACOSX/*'
site.zip
